points_lost": 0.29, "best": "pass"}], "review": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "title": "Seesaw on the Seventh Rank", "summary": "GPT-6.1 Sol, playing White, beat the 20k by W+2 after two passes. Both sides threw away 6-point swings in the middle game around G7 and D7, and the game turned when the 20k's D4 on move 25 dropped Black's lead from -3.0 to -8.4. After that, the endgame was nearly quiet, and the engine had White ahead by 2.0 at the end.", "moments": [{"turn": 12, "text": "G8 lost 4.7 points and swung Black's lead from -1.6 to +3.1. The engine preferred H7. It was the first big slip on a board where White's G7 stone was already squeezed between Black's F7 and G6."}, {"turn": 15, "text": "The 20k's J7 lost 6.4 points and took Black's lead from -0.1 to -6.5. The engine wanted C5 there, and Black gave back everything it had just won."}, {"turn": 18, "text": "C8 lost 6.5 points and gave Black's lead back, from -6.6 to -0.1. The engine's choice was E2. After White's wall along row 8 and Black's wall along row 7, both sides were trading big errors."}, {"turn": 25, "text": "D4 was the 20k's costliest move of the late game: it lost 5.4 points and moved Black's lead from -3.0 to -8.4. The engine's choice was D2. This is where White's winning margin was set."}, {"turn": 26, "text": "D3 recovered only part of the damage, and the move lost 3.6 points with Black's lead moving from -8.4 to -4.7. The engine wanted H6, but White's lower-left stones held on, and Black stayed behind through the quiet endgame."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "The inspect/candidate/audit functions in commands 4-48 only parse the current board, compute chains, liberties, empty regions and the capture result of a single move the player named by hand (e.g. p=\"C7\"), and the other commands only play moves, replay the actual game record, and write notes and SGF files. Nothing loops over empty points to score them, plays out continuations, or ranks moves, and current-position